<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40503" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕbellĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				renewal of war</i> (by the conquered party), <i>a
				revolt</i>, <i>rebellion</i> (good prose; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">defectio, seditio): rebellio facta post
					deditionem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 3, 10</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 30</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">4, 38: parare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 55</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coeptare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">comprimere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					2, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad rebellionem spectare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 2,
					18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad rebellionem compellere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 9,
					41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nihil rebellionis timere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2,
					16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Germaniae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trium principum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Vesp. 1</span></i>
			.— In plur.: multis
			Carthaginiensium rebellionibus, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Scaur.
				19, 42</span></i>.</div>
